  "raw_text": "25\n\nAndat\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nHandat\n\nAndris\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nA\nndres\n,\n \nArins\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \norange\n \n/\n \nnaranja\n\nAndris laya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \norange juice\n \n/\n \njugo de naranja\n\nAndris mapla\n \n–\n \norange\n \ncolor\n \n/\n \ncolor\n \nnaranja\n\nAngkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto bake, to burn, to set on fire, to roast, to turn on (\nex:\n \na switch)\n \n/ hornear, quemar, prender fuego, asar,\nencender (ej: un interruptor)\n\n(Note/Nota: Used on jw.org to turn on a feature / Se usa en jw.org para activar una función)\n\nAyan angkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto turn on an iron\n \n/ encender una plancha\n\nBrit\n \n(a/t:\n \nBred\n)\n \nangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto bake bread\n \n/ hornear pan\n\nKîa pain angkaia ba\n \n(Alt:\n \nIsintka\n;\n \nKîa pain batanka sunukira ba\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nincense\n \n/ incienso\n\nWîna angkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto roast meat\n \n/ asar carne\n\nAni\n \n–\n \nwhatever, whichever\n \n/\n \nlo que sea,\n \ncualquiera\n\nAni?\n \n–\n \nwhich?, what?\n \n/ ¿cual?, ¿que?\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu-12/19\n):\n \nBaibil ra ani tikska nani marikisa yawan wark karna daukaia?\n \n–\n \nIn the Bible, which texts show that we\nare to do hard work?\n \n/ En la Biblia, ¿qué textos muestran que debemos trabajar duro?)\n\nAni ani\n \n–\n \nany, whatever, whichever\n \n/\n \ncualquiera, lo que sea\n\nAni ani ra\n \n–\n \nwherever, anywhere\n \n/ donde sea\n\nAni ba\n \n–\n \nwhatever the, whichever the\n \n/ cualquiera que sea el\n\nAni ba?\n \n–\n \nwhich?, which one?, what one?\n \n/ ¿cuál ?\n\nAni mata?\n \n–\n \nto where?\n \n/\n \n¿\na\n \nd\nó\nnde?\n\nAni piua\n \n–\n \nwhatever time, whenever\n \n/\n \na cualquier hora, cuando sea\n\nAni piua ra?\n \n–\n \nAt what time?, At what point in time?, When?\n \n/ Cuando?, A qué hora?, En qué momento?\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-08/21\n):\n \nAni piua ra Jehova ra bîla kaikaia nit sa?\n \n–\n \nWhen do we need to wait on Jehovah?\n \n/ ¿Cuándo debemos\nesperar en Jehová?)\n\nAni ra\n \n(a/t:\n \nAnira;\n \nslang/argot:\n \nAnsa ra / Ansara\n)\n \n–\n \nto where, at where, to which, at which\n \n/ a dónde, a qué\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nani pliska ra\n \n–\n \nat what place\n \n/ en qué lugar)\n\nAni ra?\n \n(a/t: slang/argot:\n \nAnsara?\n)\n \n–\n \nWhere?\n \n/ ¿Dónde?\n\nAni ra sa?\n \n–\n \nWhere is it?\n \n/ ¿Dónde está?\n\nAni ra wan?\n \n–\n \nWhere did he/she/it go?\n \n/ ¿A dónde se fué?\n\nAni uplika\n \n–\n \nwhoever\n, any person who\n \n/\n \nquien sea, cualquier\n \npersona que\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb-Jan 3:16\n):\n \nani uplika witin ra kasak lukbia ba\n \n–\n \nany person who will have faith in him\n \n/ cualquier persona que\ntenga fe en él)\n\nAni uplika ra\n \n–\n \nwhomever, any person whom\n \n/\n \nquien sea, cualquier persona que\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n09/19\n):\n \nJehova ani uplika ra latwan kaiki ba wapni mangkisa\n \n–\n \nJehovah corrects any person whom he loves\n \n/\n\nJehová corrige a cualquier persona a quien ama\n)\n\nAni wina\n \n–\n \nfrom where, source\n \n/ de donde, fuente\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nvi-wsb\n):\n \nYawan ani wina bali sa?\n \n–\n \nWhere did we come from?\n \n/ ¿De dónde vinimos?)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu-09/19\n):\n \nKwâra tara uplika nani ba ani wina bal takisa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhere is the great crowd coming from?\n \n/\n \n¿De\ndónde viene la gran muchedumbre?)\n\nAnik\n \n–\n \nBy where?, Through where?\n \n/ ¿Por dónde?, ¿Por cuál parte?\n\nAnira\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nAni ra\n\nAnsa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nanswer\n \n/\n \nrespuesta\n\n(Construct:\n \nAnsiki\n;\n \nAnsikam\n;\n \nAnsika\n)\n\n(Note/Nota\n: Th\ne\n \nword\n \nAnsika\n \nis not used in all communities /\n \nL\na palabra\n \nAnsika\n \nno se usa en todas las comunidades)\n\nAnsa munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto answer, to reply\n \n/ responder\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-06/19\n):\n \nAisi kaiki ba ra, wan sinska ra naha makabi walanka nani ba ansa munaia sip sa “ya”, “d\nî\na”, “anira”,\n“ahkia”, “nahki”, bara “d\nîa\n \nmuni”.\n \n–\n \nIn the reading,\n \nin our mind we can answer the questions “who”, “what”, “where”,\n“when”, “how” and “why”\n.\n \n/ En la lectura, en nuestra mente podemos responder las preguntas \"quién\", \"qué\", \"dónde\",\n\"cuándo\", \"cómo\" y \"por qué\".)\n\nAnsa\n \n–\n \nslang form of / forma de argot de:\n \nAni\n\nAnsara\n \n/\n \nAnsa ra\n \n(slang form of / forma de argot de:\n \nAni\n \nra\n \n/\n \nAnira\n)\n \n–\n \nto where, at where, to which, at which\n \n/ a dónde,\na qué\n\nAnti\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \naunt\n \n/ tía\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nTahti\n \n–\n \nuncle\n \n/ tío)",
